WEBVTT

00:00:01.944 --> 00:00:05.544
AutoSUT derives the environment that a campaign needs.

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:12.032
Its local planning interface loads the pinned procedural plan for campaign C0045,

00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:12.882
ShadowRay.

00:00:16.872 --> 00:00:22.360
Resolve environment requirements verifies the content hash and derives eleven requirements.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:26.447
Linux is the selected platform, and platform coverage is complete.

00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:31.835
The banner states that service readiness and target effects still require a laboratory run.

00:00:34.294 --> 00:00:37.419
The environment map groups the steps by where they run:

00:00:37.707 --> 00:00:42.757
one on the attacker side, two at the exposed boundary, and seven on the target system.

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:44.882
Each zone lists what it must provide.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.015
Requirements labelled rule come from declared rules,

00:00:50.128 --> 00:00:52.728
such as a reachable public-facing application.

00:00:53.003 --> 00:00:55.265
The others come directly from STIX fields.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.228
The table keeps each source and rationale.

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:07.044
Download planning JSON saves the verified input and the requirements.

00:01:07.307 --> 00:01:10.919
The operational status is not run: nothing was provisioned.

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.553
Running a campaign is a separate step.

00:01:14.815 --> 00:01:18.665
Next, an edited capture of an earlier controlled Docker replay.

00:01:20.725 --> 00:01:24.862
From the artifact directory, run the replay and the validator shown here.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.553
This recording skips the idle time between results.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.130
The first run checks the Docker lab.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.407
The evidence-backed row shows six out of six adapted actions.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:49.172
The ShadowRay surrogate shows evidence for ten out of ten actions.

00:01:51.168 --> 00:01:53.368
Look for controlled state contract OK.

00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:59.463
The manifest check confirms that the released files match their recorded sizes and hashes.
